# 基础词 Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit01核心词汇

{{abandon}}{/əˈbændən/}{{v. 放弃；抛弃；n. 放纵}}{{He abandoned his plan to travel abroad.}}
{{ability}}{/əˈbɪləti/}{{n. 能力；才能}}{{She has the ability to solve complex problems.}}
{{able}}{/ˈeɪbl/}{{adj. 有能力的；能干的}}{{He is able to speak three languages.}}
{{abnormal}}{/æbˈnɔːrml/}{{adj. 异常的；不正常的}}{{The test results showed abnormal patterns.}}
{{aboard}}{/əˈbɔːrd/}{{adv./prep. 在船（车、飞机）上}}{{All passengers are now aboard the plane.}}
{{abolish}}{/əˈbɒlɪʃ/}{{v. 废除；取消}}{{The government decided to abolish the old law.}}
{{about}}{/əˈbaʊt/}{{prep. 关于；adv. 大约}}{{The book is about the history of China.}}
{{above}}{/əˈbʌv/}{{prep. 在…上面；adv. 在上面}}{{The temperature is above average today.}}
{{abroad}}{/əˈbrɔːd/}{{adv. 在国外}}{{She went abroad to study medicine.}}
{{absence}}{/ˈæbsəns/}{{n. 缺席；不在}}{{His absence from the meeting was noticed.}}
{{absent}}{/ˈæbsənt/}{{adj. 缺席的；不在的}}{{Three students were absent from class today.}}
{{absolute}}{/ˈæbsəluːt/}{{adj. 绝对的；完全的}}{{I have absolute confidence in her ability.}}
{{absorb}}{/əbˈzɔːrb/}{{v. 吸收；吸引}}{{Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air.}}
{{abstract}}{/ˈæbstrækt/}{{adj. 抽象的；n. 摘要}}{{The concept is too abstract for children to understand.}}
{{abundant}}{/əˈbʌndənt/}{{adj. 丰富的；充裕的}}{{The region has abundant natural resources.}}
{{abuse}}{/əˈbjuːz/}{{v./n. 滥用；虐待}}{{The abuse of power is a serious problem.}}
{{academic}}{/ˌækəˈdemɪk/}{{adj. 学术的；学院的}}{{She pursued an academic career in physics.}}
{{accelerate}}{/əkˈseləreɪt/}{{v. 加速；促进}}{{The car accelerated quickly on the highway.}}
{{accept}}{/əkˈsept/}{{v. 接受；承认}}{{She accepted the job offer happily.}}
{{access}}{/ˈækses/}{{n. 进入；通道；v. 访问}}{{Students have access to the library 24 hours a day.}}
{{accident}}{/ˈæksɪdənt/}{{n. 事故；意外}}{{The car accident caused a traffic jam.}}
{{accommodate}}{/əˈkɒmədeɪt/}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accompany}}{/əˈkʌmpəni/}{{v. 陪伴；伴随}}{{She accompanied her friend to the hospital.}}
{{accomplish}}{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/}{{v. 完成；实现}}{{He accomplished his goal of running a marathon.}}
{{according}}{/əˈkɔːrdɪŋ/}{{adv. 按照；根据}}{{According to the report, sales increased by 10%.}}
{{account}}{/əˈkaʊnt/}{{n. 账户；描述；v. 解释}}{{Please open a bank account as soon as possible.}}
{{accumulate}}{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/}{{v. 积累；积聚}}{{Dust accumulates quickly on the shelves.}}
{{accurate}}{/ˈækjərət/}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the event.}}
{{accuse}}{/əˈkjuːz/}{{v. 指控；指责}}{{He was accused of stealing the money.}}
{{accustom}}{/əˈkʌstəm/}{{v. 使习惯}}{{It took time to accustom himself to the new environment.}}
{{achieve}}{/əˈtʃiːv/}{{v. 实现；取得}}{{She achieved great success in her career.}}
{{acknowledge}}{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/}{{v. 承认；致谢}}{{He acknowledged his mistake and apologized.}}
{{acquaintance}}{/əˈkweɪntəns/}{{n. 熟人；认识}}{{He is just an acquaintance, not a close friend.}}
{{acquire}}{/əˈkwaɪər/}{{v. 获得；学到}}{{She acquired a new skill through practice.}}
{{across}}{/əˈkrɒs/}{{prep./adv. 穿过；在对面}}{{The bridge across the river is very long.}}
{{act}}{/ækt/}{{v. 行动；表演；n. 行为；法案}}{{The new act was passed by Congress last year.}}
{{adapt}}{/əˈdæpt/}{{v. 适应；改编}}{{It took him a while to adapt to the new school.}}
{{add}}{/æd/}{{v. 增加；补充}}{{Please add some sugar to the coffee.}}
{{address}}{/əˈdres/}{{n. 地址；演讲；v. 处理}}{{The president addressed the nation on television.}}
{{adequate}}{/ˈædɪkwət/}{{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The supply is adequate for our needs.}}
